Riptide's MUI layer, as Alice68-Network uses it
================================================

Alice68-Network (amiga/netgui/netgui.c) looks like Riptide's preferences
editor because it is built from the same parts. These files come from
Riptide (https://github.com/farsonic/riptide), commit 4e5f73c
("Riptide 0.37: version strings"), GPL-2.0-only like Alice68's Amiga parts:

  os/amiga.h devices.h dos.h exec.h intuition.h sana2.h os_lvos.txt
                         src/amiga/os/            (unchanged)
  amiga_os.h             src/amiga/amiga_os.h     (unchanged)
  include/string.h       src/amiga/include/       (unchanged)
  rt/rt_types.h          include/rt/              (unchanged)
  startup.S link.ld libc.c
                         src/amiga/               (unchanged)
  printf.c               src/core/printf.c        (unchanged)
  tools/gen_lvos.py elf2hunk.py hunk.py
                         tools/                   (unchanged)
  prefs/mui.h            src/amiga/prefs/         (+ MUIA_String_Secret)
  prefs/mui_util.c mui_lang.c mui_ids.h mui_lvos.txt mui_classes.h mui_theme.h
                         src/amiga/prefs/         (mui_theme.h: Alice68's icon list)
  prefs/mui_theme.c      src/amiga/prefs/         (the icon table rearranged for
                                                   Alice68's pages; WiFi, traffic, sliders
                                                   and "i" icons added; no soft bold)
  prefs/mui_classes.c    src/amiga/prefs/         (the nav list's rows and headings from
                                                   rp_nav_order[]/rp_nav_head[]; titles in
                                                   the accent colour instead of bold)
  prefs/mui_thunks.S     src/amiga/prefs/         (the dispatchers not taken left out)
  prefs/mui_widgets.c    src/amiga/prefs/mui_status.c: the graph, tabs, table and
                         stext classes only (no interface view, no Status page);
                         its tags in prefs/mui_widgets.h; class making added;
                         an on/off switch class of Alice68's own
  prefs/stat_util.c/.h   src/amiga/prefs/prefs_status.c/.h: the graph history and
                         the number wording only

Written for Alice68: cmd/cmdlib.h and prefs/prefs_fields.h (small stand-ins for
Riptide's, which describe its own tools and pages).

The library calls are Riptide's generated inline functions (tools/gen_lvos.py,
register variables, as Riptide builds them). Elsewhere Alice68's 68k code calls
libraries through lvo.S instead; this directory keeps Riptide's way, which its
releases are built with.

To take a newer Riptide: copy the files above again and redo the changes in the
brackets.
